# Git commits — no Cursor co-author

When creating or amending commits in this repository:

- Do **not** add `Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>` or any Cursor/agent co-author trailer.
- Do **not** add `Co-authored-by` lines for AI tools unless the user explicitly requests a specific co-author.
- Write commit messages as plain subject + body only (what changed and why).

If a hook or tool injects a Cursor co-author line, remove it before committing.
